      "description": "Careers at S&T –\r\n    Human Resources |\n    \r\n    Missouri S&T Skip to content Back to S&T Home Apply Visit Inquire Give Campus Map Departments Find a Department View A to Z directory Search Clear No results found. View all departments For You For You Future Students S&T Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Community Family & Friends Tools & Resources Canvas Email Joe'SS My S&T MinerLink myHR Directory News Social Media Events Library Search Explore S&T Missouri S&T Human Resources Total Rewards Careers at S&T Position Management HR Updates Resources For New Employees For Faculty and Staff For Student Employees HR Forms and Documents University and Campus Policies Payroll Employee ADA About Staff Directory Contact Us hr.mst.edu Careers at S&T Careers at S&T Human Resources Careers at S&T See why working at S&T is such a rewarding career. Take a look at what some of our S&T employees have to say and explore our career offerings. Careers at S&T Life & Community in Rolla Grow at S&T Searches Left Right Notifications Contact Us Staff Directory Employee ADA Position Management Employee Resources Total Rewards Careers at S&T HR Updates University and Campus Policies Position Profiles Left Right Careers at S&T Life & Community in Rolla Grow at S&T Searches Left Right Main Content Career Opportunities Discover career opportunities for faculty, staff, students, and executive leaders all in one place. Whether you are a current employee, prospective hire, or a student, you can find roles and resources tailored to your path. Executive Searches Current executive searches Faculty Careers For current employees For prospective employees Staff Careers For current employees For prospective employees Jobs for S&T Students Join Handshake Steps for working as a student Discover What Sets S&T Apart Take a closer look at the experiences, opportunities, and achievements that define our community, from academic pathways to the people and ideas driving innovation forward. About S&T History Traditions Degrees & Programs Research What Our Employees Say Lakshmi Ponnurasan Title: Data Analyst II \"The organization provides a supportive environment with clear onboarding processes, inclusive team culture, and opportunities to learn and contribute meaningfully. I’ve felt welcomed and well-prepared in my role, which gives me confidence that new hires would also have a positive experience here.\" See what our employees say Employee Benefits and Perks Learn more about the benefits and perks that are available at S&T. Total Rewards PTO and Leave Information Moving Allowance EAP Retirement Start Strong from Day One Getting Started Guide This guide for new employees will help you review benefits, learn about the University of Missouri System, complete the preboarding process and more. View guide Application Details Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ) Q: What should I do when I'm having technical difficulties with the application? A: Please contact the Missouri S&T IT Help Desk at 573-341-4357 or call the HR Support desk. Q: What if I make a mistake on my application and need to update it? A: We encourage you to preview the application before you submit it. That will reduce the chances of submitting an application with incomplete information or typographical errors. If the posting is still active, you can withdraw your application in \"My Job Applications\" and resubmit your application with the correct information. With defined posted periods, you may not have time to correct errors and resubmit before the application deadline. Q: How can I submit a different cover letter to each position that I am applying for? A: The resume attachment can be unique for each job. If want to submit a different cover letter for each job, you can combine your cover letter and resume into a single document and upload it in the resume area. Or you can upload three different cover letters in the Cover Letter and Attachments area. Remember to name these attachments with the job opening number or job title. This will help direct hiring managers to the intended information. All files stored in the Cover Letter and Attachment section can be viewed by the hiring managers for every job for which you apply. Q: Why do the applications include a question about eligibility to work in the United States? A: The university must comply with the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986. Therefore, before you can begin work at the university you must present documents that prove your employment eligibility. If you have questions regarding acceptable documentation, please contact Human Resource Services. Q: What is voluntary self-identification, and why am I asked to complete the information? A: The human resources department maintains information regarding the diversity of the individuals who apply for work at the university. The information does not affect your prospects for employment. It is not shared with hiring managers and is treated confidentially. Q: What if I need special assistance? A: If you have special needs as defined by the Americans with Disabilities Act, notify human resources at the address listed on the web site, or call 573-341-4241during business hours. TTY users, call 1-800-735-2966. Q: What if I forget my password? A: There is an online password request process. Your password will be emailed to you if you request it. For other questions about your user name and password, contact the IT Helpdesk at 573-341-HELP (4357). Q: How long will it take for my application to be processed? A: In most cases applications are sent to the hiring department within two (2) business days of submission. Q: When will I find out whether I get an interview? A: Interviews are scheduled by hiring departments and are determined by several factors. It may be several weeks after the job is posted before interviews are scheduled. Q: I have an interview, where do I go? A: If you are contacted by phone for an interview, be sure to write down the name of the person you will be meeting and the location of your interview. Human Resource Services does not have information about when or where interviews are scheduled. If you are unsure how to get to a specific building on campus, you can refer to the campus map at www.mst.edu/map for information. Work Authorization (H1-B Visas) For more information on H-1B Visas and permanent residence, please visit our Work Authorizations page. H1-B Labor Condition Attestations (LCA) Notice of Intent to File Labor Certifications Notice of Filing Permanent Alien Labor Certification Background Checks Per university policy HR 504 any offer of employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a Criminal Background Check (CBC).  Based on the results of the CBC, an offer may be rescinded. You may not begin employment with the university until human resources receives an acceptable CBC. Support With the Application Process If you are having difficulty with the online application process, please call or email for technical assistance hrs@mst.edu or 573-341-4241 . TTY users should call through Relay Missouri at 1-800-RELAY MO (1-800-735-2966). If you are unable to pull up the job page, try switching to an alternative web browser. Mozilla Firefox and Google Chrome are the recommended browsers. For step-by-step instructions and tips, see our full application process instructions . Missouri S&T Human Resources Missouri University of Science and Technology 113 Centennial Hall, 300 W. 12th St., Rolla, MO 65409 573-341-4241 573-341-4984 (fax) hrs@mst.edu Missouri University of Science and Technology Missouri S&T, Rolla, MO 65409 800-522-0938 webmaster@mst.edu Work at S&T Accreditation University Police Our Brand S&T Alerts Giving Student Accessibility and Testing Parking Facebook Linked In Instagram All S&T Accounts Missouri S&T is an equal opportunity employer . © The Curators of the University of Missouri UM System Privacy Policy Consumer Information Terminalfour 800-522-0938 web@mst.edu Accessibility Support Missouri S&T - Missouri University of Science and Technology Missouri University of Science and Technology Close Search Search only Yes No Top Searches How to Apply Post Admission Checklist Costs & Fees Academic Dates Scholarships Advising Quick Links Directory Campus Map Current Students Parking S&T Email Giving to S&T Missouri S&T - Missouri University of Science and Technology Missouri University of Science and Technology Apply Visit Inquire Give Close Academics Menu Academics Overview of Academics Search Degrees & Programs Undergraduate Degrees Graduate Degrees Graduate Certificates Online Degrees & Certificates Pre-College Summer Programs Admissions Menu Admissions & Aid Overview of Admissions & Aid First-Time Freshman Transfer Students International Students Graduate Students Online & Distance Military Students Dual Enrollment Summer Camp Students Campus Life Menu Campus Life Overview of Campus Life Living Options Miner Athletics Student Organizations Recreation Design Teams The Rolla Community Research Menu Research Overview of Research Office of Research & Innovation Faculty Experts Research Core Research News Innovation & Entrepreneurship University Libraries For You Future Students S&T Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Community Family & Friends Quick Links Social Events News Campus Map Directory The S&T Store About S&T Overview Rankings Leadership Giving S&T Alerts Work at S&T Facebook Instagram Linked In Twitter Youtube Discord TikTok All S&T Accounts Learn how Missouri S&T is Solving For Tomorrow Missouri S&T 800-522-0938 web@mst.edu Policies Privacy"
